<title>UK: Bulker offloading sugar after collision.</title>
<headline>Bulker offloading sugar after collision.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cypriot-flag bulk carrier Theodoros S. is offloading its cargo of 20,000 tonnes of raw sugar before docking for repairs following a collision, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Friday.</p>
<p>The 27,023-dwt vessel was holed in mid-March when it was in collision with the 33,423-dwt Turkish-registered Gulsum Ana off Malaga, Spain.</p>
<p>Its cargo of sugar was being transferred to the Cyprus-flag bulker Spiros C, with the operation expected to take until next week to complete.</p>
</text>
